{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["The reason for <b>תָּמִים תִּהְיֶה עִם יהוה אֱלֹהֶיךָ</b> is that we unify our heart to Him alone and believe that He alone does everything, and He is the One who knows the truth of all that is future, and from Him alone do we seek the future things through His prophets or through the men of His pious ones — that is to say, the Urim and Tumim — and we do not seek from those who read the heavens or from their diviners, nor do we trust that their words will come about in any case. Rather, if we hear a thing from them, we say that all is in the hands of Heaven, for He is the Elohim of gods and Most High over all, able in all, changing the courses of the stars and constellations according to His will, frustrating the signs of liars and making diviners foolish, and we believe that all that is to come will be according to a person's drawing near to His service. Therefore, after the warning against seeking the future from a diviner and one who inquires of the dead, He said that you shall be תמים with HaShem in all these things, and not fear a teller of the future, but from His prophet shall you seek and to him shall you listen. This is the view of Onkelos (Onkelos on Deuteronomy 18:13): שְׁלִים תְּהֵא בְּדַחְלְתָא דַּיְיָ אֱלָהָךְ — that you should not be lacking in fear of Him, for <b>תָּמִים</b> is one who is complete in a thing, like שֶׂה תָמִים (Exodus 12:5), which has no blemish and no deficiency whatsoever. And this is a positive commandment. And I have already mentioned this in the verse וֶהְיֵה תָמִים (Genesis 17:1)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "The Hebrew reads מאנשי חסידיו; rendered literally as 'the men of His pious ones.' The phrase אנשי חסידיו is unusual; it may be a genitive construction meaning 'men of His pious ones' or perhaps 'men of HisHasidim.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:51:35.947829567Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}